If reposTools is looking for things in the release 1.5 directory, then 
you have a very outdated version of R as well as BioC packages (I think 
R-2.0.X, which is about 1.5 years out of date). You should upgrade to 
R-2.2.1 at the very least and install current BioC packages. Given that 
R-2.3.0 is being released imminently, you might go ahead and get 
R-2.3.0beta and the devel versions of BioC.

